</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">This setup trains a total of 120 model configurations. For <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=10^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have 24 more runs.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F15" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2606.14259v1/gap_i21k_vit_wd1e-3_tr_loss_ema.svg" id="A2.F15.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:381/132;" width="381" height="132"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2606.14259v1/gap_i21k_vit_wd1e-4_tr_loss_ema.svg" id="A2.F15.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:286/134;" width="286" height="134"></object></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F15.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 15</span>: </span><span id="A2.F15.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">ViT model trained on I21K with <em id="A2.F15.5.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">independent</em> weight decay <math id="A2.F15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wortsman et al., 2024</a>]</cite>. We observe the same trend as <a href="#S1.F1" title="In 1 Introduction ‣ Beyond a Single Explanation of the Adam–SGD Gap" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, that is the optimizer advantage shifts from SGD <math id="A2.F15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math> Adam as the batch size scales.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">GPT on FineWeb.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Similarly to <a href="#A1.SS3" title="A.3 Experiments on FineWeb ‣ Appendix A Experimental details ‣ Beyond a Single Explanation of the Adam–SGD Gap" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>, we use a GPT model (see <a href="#A1.SS2" title="A.2 Architectures ‣ Appendix A Experimental details ‣ Beyond a Single Explanation of the Adam–SGD Gap" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>) trained on FineWeb 1B tokens. We use <span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">bfloat16</span> precision, 10% linear warmup with cosine scheduler to 0, and global norm clipping to 1 for both Adam and SGD. We use <em id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">independent</em> weight decay <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wortsman et al., 2024</a>]</cite>, which is decoupled and independent of learning rate <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We tune the learning rate <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, momentum <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, and batch size <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, also adding the weight decay <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<ul id="A2.I2" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">SGD (32 runs)</p>
<table id="A2.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\eta,\beta,B,\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\eta,\beta,B,\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex84.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\in\{10^{-2},10^{-1},10^{0},10^{1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in\{10^{-2},10^{-1},10^{0},10^{1}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
