<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">This setup trains a total of 64 model configurations.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F16" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2606.14259v1/gap_fineweb_wd_rustem_tr_loss_ema.svg" id="A2.F16.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:286/134;" width="286" height="134"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F16.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 16</span>: </span><span id="A2.F16.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">GPT model trained on FineWeb with <em id="A2.F16.5.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">independent</em> weight decay <math id="A2.F16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=1e-4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=1e-4</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wortsman et al., 2024</a>]</cite>. We observe the same trend as <a href="#S1.F1" title="In 1 Introduction ‣ Beyond a Single Explanation of the Adam–SGD Gap" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, that is the optimizer advantage shifts from SGD to Adam as the batch size scales.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Effect of number of steps</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Throughout this paper, we presented the batch size sweep results (<a href="#S1.F1" title="In 1 Introduction ‣ Beyond a Single Explanation of the Adam–SGD Gap" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) that fix the total number of training samples (or total token budget). Here, we conduct a preliminary study of yet another axis: under fixed batch size <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, how does the Adam–SGD gap change when scaling the number of steps? We train ViT on I21K for multiple epochs. <a href="#A2.F17" title="In B.2 Effect of number of steps ‣ Appendix B Additional results ‣ Beyond a Single Explanation of the Adam–SGD Gap" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a> shows that the gap decreases towards <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=0</annotation></semantics></math> regardless of whether the initial advantage is for SGD or Adam, suggesting that more iterations reduce the gap.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F17" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2606.14259v1/gap_i21k_vit_steps.svg" id="A2.F17.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:143/131;" width="143" height="131"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F17.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 17</span>: </span><span id="A2.F17.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">ViT trained on I21K for multiple epochs under a fixed <math id="A2.F17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>. More iterations reduces <math id="A2.F17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For the experiments in <a href="#A2.F17" title="In B.2 Effect of number of steps ‣ Appendix B Additional results ‣ Beyond a Single Explanation of the Adam–SGD Gap" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>, we use the same ViT model from <a href="#A1.SS2" title="A.2 Architectures ‣ Appendix A Experimental details ‣ Beyond a Single Explanation of the Adam–SGD Gap" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a> but trained for a longer horizon. In particular, we use <span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">bfloat16</span> precision, 10% linear warmup with cosine scheduler to 0, and global norm clipping to 1 for both Adam and SGD. We train the model for 4 and 16 epochs.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Epochs 4.</span> We tune the learning rate <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, momentum <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, and batch size <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<ul id="A2.I3" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A2.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">SGD (32 runs)</p>
<table id="A2.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex92"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\eta,\beta,B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\eta,\beta,B)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex92.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\in\{10^{-2},10^{-1},10^{0},10^{1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in\{10^{-2},10^{-1},10^{0},10^{1}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex93"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\times\{0.9,0.95,0.99,0.999\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.95</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.99</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.999</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\times\{0.9,0.95,0.99,0.999\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex94"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\times\{1024,4096\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1024</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4096</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\times\{1024,4096\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Adam (32 runs) (<math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}=\beta_{2}=\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}=\beta_{2}=\beta</annotation></semantics></math>)</p>
<table id="A2.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex95"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\eta,\beta,B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\eta,\beta,B)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex95.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\in\{10^{-4},10^{-3},10^{-2},10^{-1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in\{10^{-4},10^{-3},10^{-2},10^{-1}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex96"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\times\{0.9,0.95,0.99,0.999\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.95</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.99</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.999</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\times\{0.9,0.95,0.99,0.999\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex97"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\times\{1024,4096\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1024</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4096</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\times\{1024,4096\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Epochs 16.</span> We tune the learning rate <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, momentum <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, and batch size <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<ul id="A2.I4" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A2.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">SGD (18 runs)</p>
<table id="A2.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex98"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
