</div>
<figure id="A2.F18" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2606.14259v1/gap_i21k_resnet50_ep4_tr_loss_ema.svg" id="A2.F18.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:381/126;" width="381" height="126"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F18.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 18</span>: </span><span id="A2.F18.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">ResNet50 trained on I21K for 4 epochs across <math id="A2.F18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that even at a large <math id="A2.F18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=65536" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>65536</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=65536</annotation></semantics></math>, SGD still has the advantage, suggesting a gap floor that depends on the architecture an data.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Effect of independent <math id="A2.SS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>s</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To ablate our prior results that rely on <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\beta_{1}=\beta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\beta_{1}=\beta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Orvieto and Gower, 2025</a>]</cite>, we run independent <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>s sweep at small batch size. We use the same setup as <a href="#A1.SS3" title="A.3 Experiments on FineWeb ‣ Appendix A Experimental details ‣ Beyond a Single Explanation of the Adam–SGD Gap" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We tune the learning rate <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and batch size <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A2.I6" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A2.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Adam (240 runs) (<math id="A2.I6.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}\neq\beta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}\neq\beta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>)</p>
<table id="A2.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex110"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\eta,\beta_{1},\beta_{2},B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\eta,\beta_{1},\beta_{2},B)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex110.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\in\{3\cdot 10^{-5},10^{-4},3\cdot 10^{-4},10^{-3},3\cdot 10^{-3}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in\{3\cdot 10^{-5},10^{-4},3\cdot 10^{-4},10^{-3},3\cdot 10^{-3}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex111"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\times\{0.9,0.95,0.99,0.999\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.95</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.99</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.999</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\times\{0.9,0.95,0.99,0.999\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex112"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\times\{0.9,0.95,0.99,0.999,0.9999,0.99999\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.95</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.99</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.999</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.9999</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.99999</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\times\{0.9,0.95,0.99,0.999,0.9999,0.99999\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex113"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\times\{1,16\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\times\{1,16\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A2.F19" title="In B.3 Effect of independent 𝛽s ‣ Appendix B Additional results ‣ Beyond a Single Explanation of the Adam–SGD Gap" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a> shows that at <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=16</annotation></semantics></math>, a large <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{2}=0.999" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.999</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{2}=0.999</annotation></semantics></math> leads to similar performance as SGD. The same is observed for <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=1</annotation></semantics></math> but requiring an even larger <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{2}=0.9999" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9999</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{2}=0.9999</annotation></semantics></math>. At first glance, this seems in contrast with prior results showing that SGD outperforms Adam at small <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> for this setup. Note however, that Adam with a <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{2}\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{2}\to 1</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds essentially to SGD.
Since SGD is optimal under small <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=1</annotation></semantics></math>, Adam with <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{2}\approx 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≈</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{2}\approx 1</annotation></semantics></math> approximates SGD, suppressing its adaptivity.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F19" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2606.14259v1/gap_fineweb_betas_bs16_tr_loss_ema.svg" id="A2.F19.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/132;" width="476" height="132"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2606.14259v1/gap_fineweb_betas_bs1_tr_loss_ema.svg" id="A2.F19.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/132;" width="476" height="132"></object></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F19.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 19</span>: </span><span id="A2.F19.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">GPT trained on FineWeb with independent <math id="A2.F19.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>s at <math id="A2.F19.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.F19.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=16</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Large scale GPT and ViT</h3>

<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We extend results in the main paper with larger scale architectures, showing that the <em id="A2.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">crossover</em> batch size is observed even for larger scale GPT and ViT architectures.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GPT 250M on FineWeb 5BT.</span> Same setup as <a href="#A1.SS3" title="A.3 Experiments on FineWeb ‣ Appendix A Experimental details ‣ Beyond a Single Explanation of the Adam–SGD Gap" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a> but larger scale. The GPT here has 24 layers, 12 heads, 768 embed size, and 1024 seq length. We tune the learning rate <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, and batch size <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A2.I7" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A2.I7.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I7.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I7.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">SGD (64 runs)</p>
<table id="A2.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex114"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\eta,\beta,B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\eta,\beta,B)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex114.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\in\{10^{-2},10^{-1},10^{0},10^{1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in\{10^{-2},10^{-1},10^{0},10^{1}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex115"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex115.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\times\{0.9,0.95,0.99,0.999\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.95</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.99</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.999</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\times\{0.9,0.95,0.99,0.999\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
