</div>
<figure id="A2.F22" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2606.14259v1/gap_hg38_char_bs1_tr_loss_ema.svg" id="A2.F22.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:286/134;" width="286" height="134"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F22.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 22</span>: </span><span id="A2.F22.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">GPT trained on HG38 at smallest batch size still presents Adam<math id="A2.F22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&gt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;</annotation></semantics></math>SGD.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.6 </span>Validation performance gap</h3>

<div id="A2.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Throughout this work, we have focused on training loss. Here, we report the gap in generalization performance. These are the same models from <a href="#S1.F1" title="In 1 Introduction ‣ Beyond a Single Explanation of the Adam–SGD Gap" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, that is GPT from <a href="#A1.SS3" title="A.3 Experiments on FineWeb ‣ Appendix A Experimental details ‣ Beyond a Single Explanation of the Adam–SGD Gap" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a> and ViT from <a href="#A1.SS4" title="A.4 Experiments on ImageNet21K ‣ Appendix A Experimental details ‣ Beyond a Single Explanation of the Adam–SGD Gap" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F23" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2606.14259v1/gap_i21k_vit_vl_acc.svg" id="A2.F23.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/166;" width="476" height="166"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F23.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 23</span>: </span><span id="A2.F23.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Top-1 validation accuracy of ViT model trained on I21K. We observe the same trend as <a href="#S1.F1" title="In 1 Introduction ‣ Beyond a Single Explanation of the Adam–SGD Gap" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, that is the optimizer advantage shifts from SGD <math id="A2.F23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math> Adam as the batch size scales.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A2.F24" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2606.14259v1/gap_fineweb_vl_loss.svg" id="A2.F24.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/165;" width="476" height="165"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F24.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 24</span>: </span><span id="A2.F24.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Validation loss of GPT model of 50M parameters trained on FineWeb 1B tokens. We observe the same trend as <a href="#S1.F1" title="In 1 Introduction ‣ Beyond a Single Explanation of the Adam–SGD Gap" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, that is the optimizer advantage shifts from SGD <math id="A2.F24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math> Adam as the batch size scales.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.7 </span>Architecture interpolation with independent components</h3>

<div id="A2.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Same experimental settings as <a href="#A1.SS10" title="A.10 Experiments on architecture interpolation ‣ Appendix A Experimental details ‣ Beyond a Single Explanation of the Adam–SGD Gap" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.10</span></a>, including the learning rate <math id="A2.SS7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> and momentum <math id="A2.SS7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> tuning grid.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We tune the learning rate <math id="A2.SS7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, momentum <math id="A2.SS7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, and batch size <math id="A2.SS7.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<ul id="A2.I10" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A2.I10.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I10.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I10.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">SGD (12 runs)</p>
<table id="A2.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex132"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex132.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\eta,\beta,B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\eta,\beta,B)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex132.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\in\{10^{-2},10^{-1},10^{0}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>0</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in\{10^{-2},10^{-1},10^{0}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex133"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex133.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\times\{0.9,0.95,0.99,0.999\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.95</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.99</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.999</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\times\{0.9,0.95,0.99,0.999\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex134"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex134.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\times\{1024\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1024</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\times\{1024\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I10.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I10.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I10.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Adam (12 runs) (<math id="A2.I10.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}=\beta_{2}=\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}=\beta_{2}=\beta</annotation></semantics></math>):</p>
<table id="A2.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex135"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex135.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\eta,\beta,B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\eta,\beta,B)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex135.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\in\{10^{-4},10^{-3},10^{-2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in\{10^{-4},10^{-3},10^{-2}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex136"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex136.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\times\{0.9,0.95,0.99,0.999\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.95</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.99</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.999</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\times\{0.9,0.95,0.99,0.999\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex137"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex137.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\times\{1024\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1024</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\times\{1024\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A2.T4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 4</span>: </span><span id="A2.T4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Single architecture-choice ablation (L: LayerNorm, G: GeLU, and D: Depthwise) at <math id="A2.T4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1024</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=1024</annotation></semantics></math>. Each individual modification slightly moves the advantage towards Adam. However, as we have seen in <a href="#S4.T2" title="In 4.3 Dissecting architectural components ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Beyond a Single Explanation of the Adam–SGD Gap" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, the cumulative effect is even stronger. The <math id="A2.T4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> measures the difference between the best run trained with SGD and Adam (<math id="A2.T4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> means Adam has lower loss).
<br class="ltx_break"></span></figcaption>
<table id="A2.T4.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A2.T4.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
