</table>
</figure>
<div id="A2.SS7.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This setup trains a total of 72 model configurations, as there are 3 configurations in <a href="#A2.T4" title="In B.7 Architecture interpolation with independent components ‣ Appendix B Additional results ‣ Beyond a Single Explanation of the Adam–SGD Gap" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.8 </span>Isolating early training phase with <span id="A2.SS8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">stable_sgd</span> shared trajectory</h3>

<div id="A2.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Same setup as in <a href="#A1.SS11" title="A.11 Experiments on early training phase ‣ Appendix A Experimental details ‣ Beyond a Single Explanation of the Adam–SGD Gap" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.11</span></a> but training the shared trajectory <span id="A2.SS8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">stable_sgd</span> instead of <span id="A2.SS8.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">stable_adam</span>. This shared SGD trajectory uses <math id="A2.SS8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=3\cdot 10^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=3\cdot 10^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0.95" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.95</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0.95</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We tune the learning rate <math id="A2.SS8.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, momentum <math id="A2.SS8.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, and batch size <math id="A2.SS8.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> at every branching as</p>
<ul id="A2.I11" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A2.I11.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I11.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I11.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">SGD (20 runs)</p>
<table id="A2.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex138"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex138.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\eta,\beta,B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\eta,\beta,B)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex138.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\in\{3\cdot 10^{-2},10^{-1},3\cdot 10^{-1},10^{0},3\cdot 10^{0}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in\{3\cdot 10^{-2},10^{-1},3\cdot 10^{-1},10^{0},3\cdot 10^{0}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex139"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex139.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\times\{0.9,0.95,0.99,0.999\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.95</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.99</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.999</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\times\{0.9,0.95,0.99,0.999\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex140"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex140.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\times\{1024\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1024</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\times\{1024\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I11.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I11.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I11.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Adam (20 runs) (<math id="A2.I11.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}=\beta_{2}=\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}=\beta_{2}=\beta</annotation></semantics></math>):</p>
<table id="A2.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex141"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex141.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\eta,\beta,B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\eta,\beta,B)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex141.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\in\{10^{-3},3\cdot 10^{-3},10^{-2},3\cdot 10^{-2},10^{-1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in\{10^{-3},3\cdot 10^{-3},10^{-2},3\cdot 10^{-2},10^{-1}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex142"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex142.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\times\{0.9,0.95,0.99,0.999\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.95</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.99</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.999</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\times\{0.9,0.95,0.99,0.999\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex143"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex143.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\times\{1024\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1024</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\times\{1024\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This setup trains a total of 280 model configurations, as there are 7 branches.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F25" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A2.F25.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2606.14259v1/split_tinystories_sgd.svg" id="A2.F25.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/397;" width="476" height="397"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F25.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="A2.F25.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Overparametrized w/ TinyStories</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A2.F25.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2606.14259v1/split_fineweb_sgd.svg" id="A2.F25.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/408;" width="476" height="408"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F25.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="A2.F25.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Underparametrized w/ FineWeb</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F25.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 25</span>: </span><span id="A2.F25.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">GPT model of 50M parameters trained on (a) 10M TinyStories tokens for 80 epochs and (b) 1B FineWeb tokens for 1 epoch at batch size <math id="A2.F25.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1024</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=1024</annotation></semantics></math>.
We isolate the effect of early training dynamics by branching Adam and SGD from a shared constant learning rate trajectory (<span id="A2.F25.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">stable_sgd</span>).
Branching happens at different intervals to probe different stages of training. (a) For overparametrization, both branches converge to low loss as the problem is solvable with more epochs, while (b) for underparametrization, SGD lags behind.
For every branch, the momentum state is reset, and the learning rate <math id="A2.F25.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> and momentum <math id="A2.F25.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> are tuned, see <a href="#A1.SS11" title="A.11 Experiments on early training phase ‣ Appendix A Experimental details ‣ Beyond a Single Explanation of the Adam–SGD Gap" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.11</span></a>.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Detailed theoretical study</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To provide theoretical evidence on why the Adam–SGD gap decreases with batch size and the potential existence of a crossover batch size, we use the non-convex convergence bounds from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kovalev, 2025</a>]</cite>, i.e., the bounds on the gradient norm. These bounds were found to have a strong predictive ability for the scaling of the algorithm’s parameters with the token budget <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib69" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shulgin et al., 2026</a>, <a href="#bib.bib70" title="" class="ltx_ref">Islamov et al., 2026</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Notation and setting</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our goal is to solve the stochastic optimization problem</p>
<table id="A3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\min_{x\in{\mathcal{X}}}\left[f(x)=\mathbb{E}_{\xi\sim{\mathcal{D}}}[f(x,\xi)]\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{x\in{\mathcal{X}}}\left[f(x)=\mathbb{E}_{\xi\sim{\mathcal{D}}}[f(x,\xi)]\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the space <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> is equipped with an inner product <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left&lt;\cdot,\cdot\right&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left&lt;\cdot,\cdot\right&gt;</annotation></semantics></math> and a norm <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|</annotation></semantics></math>, which need not be the norm induced by this inner product. To solve <a href="#A3.E2" title="In C.1 Notation and setting ‣ Appendix C Detailed theoretical study ‣ Beyond a Single Explanation of the Adam–SGD Gap" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we use the Stochastic Trust-Region Gradient Method, summarized in <a href="#alg1" title="In C.2 Convergence bounds ‣ Appendix C Detailed theoretical study ‣ Beyond a Single Explanation of the Adam–SGD Gap" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. Depending on the choice of <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|</annotation></semantics></math>, this framework recovers several practical optimization algorithms. For example, when <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|=\|\cdot\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|=\|\cdot\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the update in <a href="#alg1" title="In C.2 Convergence bounds ‣ Appendix C Detailed theoretical study ‣ Beyond a Single Explanation of the Adam–SGD Gap" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> reduces to</p>
<table id="A3.Ex144" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex144.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{k+1}=x_{k}-\eta\frac{m_{k+1}}{\|m_{k+1}\|_{2}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{k+1}=x_{k}-\eta\frac{m_{k+1}}{\|m_{k+1}\|_{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">which corresponds to a step of normalized SGD (NSGD) with momentum. When <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|=\|\cdot\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|=\|\cdot\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>, the update recovers SignSGD with momentum,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex145" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex145.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{k+1}=x_{k}-\eta\mathrm{sign}(m_{k+1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>sign</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{k+1}=x_{k}-\eta\mathrm{sign}(m_{k+1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">In our experiments, we approximate the convergence behavior of SGD with momentum and clipping by that of normalized SGD with momentum. Similarly, we use SignSGD with momentum as a proxy for Adam, motivated by their empirical similarity <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Orvieto and Gower, 2025</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Convergence bounds</h3>

<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Stochastic Trust-region Gradient Method with Momentum</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> norm <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|</annotation></semantics></math>, step size <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, momentum <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, number of iterations <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\in\{1,2,\dots\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\in\{1,2,\dots\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1,\dots,K-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1,\dots,K-1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              Sample <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{k}\in{\mathcal{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{k}\in{\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              Compute <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="m_{k+1}=(1-\alpha)m_{k}+\alpha\nabla f(x_{k},\xi_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{k+1}=(1-\alpha)m_{k}+\alpha\nabla f(x_{k},\xi_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              Compute <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{k+1}=\mathrm{argmin}_{d}\left&lt;d,m_{k+1}\right&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>argmin</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{k+1}=\mathrm{argmin}_{d}\left&lt;d,m_{k+1}\right&gt;</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|d\|\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|d\|\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              Update <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{k+1}=x_{k}-\eta d_{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{k+1}=x_{k}-\eta d_{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
             return

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Assuming that</p>
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla f(x)-\nabla f(y)\|_{*}\leq L\|x-y\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla f(x)-\nabla f(y)\|_{*}\leq L\|x-y\|</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">there exists <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x\|_{*}\leq\rho\|x\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x\|_{*}\leq\rho\|x\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">there exists <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\xi\sim{\mathcal{D}}}[\|\nabla f(x,\xi)-\nabla f(x)\|^{2}_{2}]\leq\frac{\sigma^{2}}{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\xi\sim{\mathcal{D}}}[\|\nabla f(x,\xi)-\nabla f(x)\|^{2}_{2}]\leq\frac{\sigma^{2}}{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> is the batch size,</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kovalev [2025]</a></cite> provide the following non-convex bounds</p>
<table id="A3.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex146"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex146.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{1\leq k\leq K}\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla f(x_{k})\|_{*}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{1\leq k\leq K}\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla f(x_{k})\|_{*}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex146.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim\frac{\delta_{0}}{\eta K}+\frac{\rho\sigma}{\alpha\sqrt{B}K}+\frac{\sqrt{\alpha}\rho\sigma}{\sqrt{B}}+L\eta+\frac{L\eta}{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>B</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><msqrt><mi>B</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim\frac{\delta_{0}}{\eta K}+\frac{\rho\sigma}{\alpha\sqrt{B}K}+\frac{\sqrt{\alpha}\rho\sigma}{\sqrt{B}}+L\eta+\frac{L\eta}{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\delta_{0}B}{\eta T}+\frac{\rho\sigma\sqrt{B}}{\alpha T}+\frac{\sqrt{\alpha}\rho\sigma}{\sqrt{B}}+L\eta+\frac{L\eta}{\alpha}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>B</mi></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><msqrt><mi>B</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\delta_{0}B}{\eta T}+\frac{\rho\sigma\sqrt{B}}{\alpha T}+\frac{\sqrt{\alpha}\rho\sigma}{\sqrt{B}}+L\eta+\frac{L\eta}{\alpha},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of optimization steps, <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is the total budget, <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{0}=f(x_{0})-f^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{0}=f(x_{0})-f^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, and numerical constants are ignored. We use the connection <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=KB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=KB</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain the second line in <a href="#A3.E3" title="In C.2 Convergence bounds ‣ Appendix C Detailed theoretical study ‣ Beyond a Single Explanation of the Adam–SGD Gap" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. Following derivations of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib69" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shulgin et al. [2026]</a></cite> in the large <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\gg 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≫</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\gg 1</annotation></semantics></math> and small <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> regime, we obtain that the optimal <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> are</p>
<table id="A3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\propto\frac{B\delta_{0}^{3/4}}{L^{1/4}(\rho\sigma)^{1/2}T^{3/4}},\quad\alpha\propto\frac{\sqrt{L\delta_{0}}B}{\rho\sigma\sqrt{T}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∝</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∝</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>T</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\propto\frac{B\delta_{0}^{3/4}}{L^{1/4}(\rho\sigma)^{1/2}T^{3/4}},\quad\alpha\propto\frac{\sqrt{L\delta_{0}}B}{\rho\sigma\sqrt{T}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Using this choice of hyperparameters, we obtain a bound minimized with respect to both <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A3.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle U_{\|\cdot\|}=\min_{1\leq k\leq K}\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla f(x_{k})\|_{*}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></munder><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle U_{\|\cdot\|}=\min_{1\leq k\leq K}\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla f(x_{k})\|_{*}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim\frac{(L\delta_{0})^{1/4}\sqrt{\rho\sigma}}{T^{1/4}}+\frac{(\rho\sigma)^{2}}{\sqrt{L\delta_{0}TB}}+\frac{(L\delta_{0})^{3/4}B}{\sqrt{\rho\sigma}T^{3/4}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msqrt><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim\frac{(L\delta_{0})^{1/4}\sqrt{\rho\sigma}}{T^{1/4}}+\frac{(\rho\sigma)^{2}}{\sqrt{L\delta_{0}TB}}+\frac{(L\delta_{0})^{3/4}B}{\sqrt{\rho\sigma}T^{3/4}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Comparison of the bounds for NSGD and SignSGD</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Now we compare the bound equation <a href="#A3.E5" title="Equation 5 ‣ C.2 Convergence bounds ‣ Appendix C Detailed theoretical study ‣ Beyond a Single Explanation of the Adam–SGD Gap" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> for NSGD and SignSGD with momentum using the specific choice of constants. For the <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> norm, we have <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=L_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=L_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=1</annotation></semantics></math>, while for the <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>, it is <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=L_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=L_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=\sqrt{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=\sqrt{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since we solve the same problem, the noise <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is the same for both methods. Therefore, the difference in the bounds for NSGD and SignSGD with momentum is<span id="footnote5" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">5</span>
              
              
              
              
              
              
              
            We denote by <math id="footnote5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="footnote5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> the bounds obtained from equation <a href="#A3.E5" title="Equation 5 ‣ C.2 Convergence bounds ‣ Appendix C Detailed theoretical study ‣ Beyond a Single Explanation of the Adam–SGD Gap" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> with the norm chosen as <math id="footnote5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="footnote5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span></p>
<table id="A3.E6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E6X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E6X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{U}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E6X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=U_{\infty}-U_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=U_{\infty}-U_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E6Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E6Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{(\sigma^{2}\delta_{0})^{1/4}\left((L_{\infty}d)^{1/4}-L_{2}^{1/4}\right)}{T^{1/4}}+\frac{\sigma^{2}}{\sqrt{\delta_{0}TB}}\left(\frac{d}{\sqrt{L_{\infty}}}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{L_{2}}}\right)+\frac{\delta_{0}^{3/4}B}{\sqrt{\sigma}T^{3/4}}\left(\frac{L_{\infty}^{3/4}}{d^{1/4}}-L_{2}^{3/4}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><msqrt><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>σ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msubsup><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{(\sigma^{2}\delta_{0})^{1/4}\left((L_{\infty}d)^{1/4}-L_{2}^{1/4}\right)}{T^{1/4}}+\frac{\sigma^{2}}{\sqrt{\delta_{0}TB}}\left(\frac{d}{\sqrt{L_{\infty}}}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{L_{2}}}\right)+\frac{\delta_{0}^{3/4}B}{\sqrt{\sigma}T^{3/4}}\left(\frac{L_{\infty}^{3/4}}{d^{1/4}}-L_{2}^{3/4}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The derivative of the gap with respect to the batch size is given below</p>
<table id="A3.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial\Delta_{U}}{\partial B}=-\frac{\sigma^{2}}{\sqrt{\delta_{0}TB^{3}}}\left(\frac{d}{\sqrt{L_{\infty}}}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{L_{2}}}\right)+\frac{\delta_{0}^{3/4}}{\sqrt{\sigma}T^{3/4}}\left(\frac{L_{\infty}^{3/4}}{d^{1/4}}-L_{2}^{3/4}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>U</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><msqrt><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msqrt><mi>σ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msubsup><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial\Delta_{U}}{\partial B}=-\frac{\sigma^{2}}{\sqrt{\delta_{0}TB^{3}}}\left(\frac{d}{\sqrt{L_{\infty}}}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{L_{2}}}\right)+\frac{\delta_{0}^{3/4}}{\sqrt{\sigma}T^{3/4}}\left(\frac{L_{\infty}^{3/4}}{d^{1/4}}-L_{2}^{3/4}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">We observe that the gap between the two optimizers and how it changes with batch size depends on the interaction of the geometry and dimensionality of the problem. Different relations between <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{2},L_{\infty}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{2},L_{\infty},</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> can lead to different signs of the gap, as well as different dynamics with the batch size. Let us consider several cases. Note that we always have <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{2}\leq L_{\infty}\leq dL_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{2}\leq L_{\infty}\leq dL_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1}&lt;\mathbf{L}_{\bm{\infty}}/\mathbf{L_{2}}&lt;\mathbf{d^{1/3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐋</mi><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">∞</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>𝐋</mi><mn>𝟐</mn></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>𝐝</mi><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>𝟑</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}&lt;\mathbf{L}_{\bm{\infty}}/\mathbf{L_{2}}&lt;\mathbf{d^{1/3}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this scenario, we have</p>
<table id="A3.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{U}\propto\frac{1}{T^{1/4}}+\frac{1}{\sqrt{TB}}-\frac{B}{T^{3/4}},\quad\frac{\partial\Delta_{U}}{\partial B}\propto-\frac{1}{\sqrt{TB^{3}}}-\frac{1}{T^{3/4}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>U</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{U}\propto\frac{1}{T^{1/4}}+\frac{1}{\sqrt{TB}}-\frac{B}{T^{3/4}},\quad\frac{\partial\Delta_{U}}{\partial B}\propto-\frac{1}{\sqrt{TB^{3}}}-\frac{1}{T^{3/4}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We observe that the derivative of the gap is always negative. Therefore, the sign of the gap also depends on the value of the gap at <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=1</annotation></semantics></math>. If the gap at the batch size <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=1</annotation></semantics></math> is already negative, SignSGD is already favored at <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=1</annotation></semantics></math> and remains favored as <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> increases. If the gap at <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=1</annotation></semantics></math> is positive, then we will observe that there is a crossover from NSGD being better to SignSGD being better. Note that the value of the gap at <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=1</annotation></semantics></math> depends on the relation between <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{2},L_{\infty},d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{2},L_{\infty},d</annotation></semantics></math>, as well as <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. This serves as an additional support that the model, dataset, and gradient noise jointly affect the sign of the gap.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We observe that most of the experimental setups tested in our work lie in this regime, since we observe a crossover from SGD being better to Adam being better. Moreover, for the Genomics setting, we do observe that Adam is better than SGD even for a batch size <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, which is also possible according to the convergence analysis.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{d^{1/3}}&lt;\mathbf{L}_{\bm{\infty}}/\mathbf{L_{2}}&lt;\mathbf{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐝</mi><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>𝟑</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐋</mi><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">∞</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>𝐋</mi><mn>𝟐</mn></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>𝐝</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{d^{1/3}}&lt;\mathbf{L}_{\bm{\infty}}/\mathbf{L_{2}}&lt;\mathbf{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this regime, we have</p>
<table id="A3.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{U}\propto\frac{1}{T^{1/4}}+\frac{1}{\sqrt{TB}}+\frac{B}{T^{3/4}},\quad\frac{\partial\Delta_{U}}{\partial B}\propto-\frac{1}{\sqrt{TB^{3}}}+\frac{1}{T^{3/4}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>U</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{U}\propto\frac{1}{T^{1/4}}+\frac{1}{\sqrt{TB}}+\frac{B}{T^{3/4}},\quad\frac{\partial\Delta_{U}}{\partial B}\propto-\frac{1}{\sqrt{TB^{3}}}+\frac{1}{T^{3/4}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The relation between <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{2},L_{\infty}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{2},L_{\infty},</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> implies that the gap is always positive, i.e., NSGD achieves lower loss than SignSGD, and there exists a batch size <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\propto T^{1/6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>∝</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\propto T^{1/6}</annotation></semantics></math> when the gap is the smallest. This case might be linked to ResNet50/ImageNet-21K experiments, where we observe that SGD remains better than Adam even at a large batch size.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
</article>
</div>
</div>
